# RAILWAY-ONLY, LEGACY. Coolify is the primary deployment path now - see
# auto_sync/COOLIFY.md for PlayerSync/PriceSync/SBCSync's actual
# Dockerfile-based setup (dedicated Dockerfile.player/Dockerfile.price/
# Dockerfile.sbc, Scheduled Task vs continuous service, required env
# vars). This file only matters if a Railway (Nixpacks) service in this
# repo is still live; it is not read by the Coolify deployment.
#
# FUT.GG replacement pipeline.
#
# futgg_player_worker: one-shot. Run daily as a Cron Job to discover and
# refresh card metadata.
#
# futgg_price_worker: OBSOLETE - futgg_price_sync.py was the old
# per-card Playwright price scraper. futgg_bulk_price_sync.py's bulk feed
# (~27k cards from one page load vs. ~2s/card with ~26% failing - see
# that script's own docstring) replaced it; this line is commented out
# rather than removed so the "what used to run here and why it stopped"
# history stays visible. Do not re-enable on Railway without first
# checking futgg_bulk_price_sync.py is actually deployed there too.
# futgg_price_worker: python futgg_price_sync.py
#
# DATABASE_URL is the only variable it requires. Every other setting has a
# production-tuned default; override only with a measured reason.
futgg_player_worker: python futgg_player_sync.py

# Bulk price ingest: one page load harvests the whole ~27k-card price
# feed, bypassing the per-card signing endpoint that rate-limits the
# scraper. Continuous service. Dry run until FUTGG_BULK_APPLY=true
# (defaults to true in the script itself - see futgg_bulk_price_sync.py).
futgg_bulk_price_worker: python futgg_bulk_price_sync.py

# Sales history via the signed JSON endpoint. One page load for the whole
# process lifetime; every card after that is a fetch() from inside it.
futgg_sales_worker: python futgg_sales_sync.py

# FUT.GG content collector: live FC27 SBCs, exact squads and Gallery. (FUTBIN's
# Cloudflare hard-blocks every network origin tested, including Railway -
# see futgg_content_sync.py's own docstring and README.md). One-shot -
# schedule as a Railway Cron Job, not a permanent worker.
futgg_sbc_worker: python futgg_content_sync.py
